# Backend Rules

## API Routes
- Place routes in `server/api/` following RESTful naming
- Use `defineEventHandler` for all handlers
- Return consistent response shapes: `{ data }` or `{ error }`

## Error Handling
- Use `createError` from H3 for API errors with proper status codes
- Never expose internal error details to clients
- Log errors server-side before returning sanitized response

## Validation
- Validate all incoming request bodies with Zod
- Use `readValidatedBody` or validate early in handler

## Security
- Never trust client input - always validate/sanitize
- Don't expose sensitive env vars in responses
- Use proper HTTP methods (GET for reads, POST/PUT/PATCH for writes, DELETE for removal)

## Supabase
- Use server-side Supabase client for sensitive operations
- Don't expose service role key to client
- Handle Supabase errors explicitly, don't let them bubble raw
